      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T07:34:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Gerrit led the way for sure, but it\u0027s become a de facto standard for any modern git-like system: https://lobste.rs/s/aupah1/gerrit_gitbutler_jujutsu_projects\n\ntangled.org also supports them for the same reason.\n\nIt\u0027s not that calling this \"gerrit\" is wrong in our case, but a more generic name is more future proof (we will definitely have to move off of Gerrit at some point soon-ish), and it clarifies that this does not do network roundtrips to Gerrit (which other commands like gerrit_update_comment etc do)",
